{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בה' וכחש בעמיתו", :translit "baShem v'chichesh b'amito", :gloss "by Hashem and denies to his fellow"} {:he "בין בה' בין בעמיתו", :translit "bein baShem bein b'amito", :gloss "whether by Hashem whether by his fellow"} {:he "דבר שאינו יודע בו אלא הקב\"ה וחבירו", :translit "davar she'eino yode'a bo ella haKadosh Baruch Hu v'chaveiro", :gloss "a matter that none knows but the Holy One blessed be He and his fellow"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Explicates the doubled phrasing: the oath can invoke God's name or the fellow's trust."}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 5:21 describes one who sins by withholding a deposit or robbery and then 'denies it' (v'chichesh). The formulation 'by an oath and denies to his fellow' raises the question of whether the denial invokes God's name or merely deceives the fellow. Shevu'ot 38b and 45b address the parameters of oaths involving financial claims and the distinction between oaths sworn in God's name and those involving a fellow's knowledge.", :sources ["Leviticus 5:21" "Shevu'ot 38b" "Shevu'ot 45b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Explicates the doubled phrasing: the oath can invoke God's name or the fellow's trust.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:31.718499756Z", :model "glm-5.2"}